PROD-001 (print product templates: pins & magnets, plus multi-up sheets) is
implemented on branch feat/PROD-001-pins-magnets — check `gh pr list` before
assuming it's merged. The multi-up half (several products ganged up on a
Letter/A4 sheet, count capped at what fits) was asked for after the first
PR went up and rides in the same branch and PR.
Note the ids: the two product-template tickets were originally written as
TPL-001/TPL-002, which already belong to closed tickets (#23 multi-page
designs, #24 duplicate a page, and storeTypes.ts still cites TPL-001 for the
stack view). They were renumbered PROD-001/PROD-002 before any work started.

Next ticket: no auto-pickable one. What's open, each needing a decision:
- PROD-002 (further product families: stickers, cards, patches, keychains,
  totes, mugs, phone cases) — explicitly "not yet scoped" on the checklist.
  It extends PROD-001's preset model past circles, so it needs a shape
  decision first: products.ts's ProductShape is a single-member union
  ('circle') on purpose, and productGuides.ts draws arcs directly. A
  die-cut sticker or a rounded-rect card needs a path-based guide, not a
  radius.
- PHOTO-008 (sharpen, blur, noise) — a convolution pipeline, unlike every
  photo util shipped so far (toneLUT, channelLUT, levelsCurves, colorPass
  are all per-pixel or per-channel maps). Expect a kernel util and the
  first photo control that can't recompute per frame on a large image; the
  preview will likely need a downscaled proxy, the way useHistogram does.
- BOOK-001 (page templates system) — large, needs its own phasing pass.
- BOOK-004 (print export modal) — deferred by the user pending a rethink;
  don't resume without them re-raising it.

Two known boundaries left by PROD-001, both deliberate and both worth
knowing before touching this area:
- Page thumbnails (PageBar/PageStack) draw book guides but not product
  guides, so a pin page's thumbnail is a plain white square.
- Resizing the artboard (UX-014) on a product page leaves the guide circle
  at its original diameter, so the two stop agreeing. Book pages have the
  same gap with their bleed, so it wasn't singled out here.
